events.thought:
I have identified and fixed the defect. The linker error `undefined reference to '__device_dts_ord_25'` was caused by the `retainedmem` device tree node not having a `compatible` property, which is required for `DEVICE_DT_GET` to correctly identify and initialize it as a device.

I have modified the file `/zephyrproject/zephyr/tests/subsys/settings/retention/boards/qemu_cortex_m3.overlay` to add `compatible = "zephyr,retained-ram";` to the `retainedmem` node.

The change made is:
```diff
--- a/zephyr/tests/subsys/settings/retention/boards/qemu_cortex_m3.overlay
+++ b/zephyr/tests/subsys/settings/retention/boards/qemu_cortex_m3.overlay
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 	\t\t#size-cells = <1>;

 	\t\tretainedmem {
+	\t\t\tcompatible = "zephyr,retained-ram";
 	\t\t\tstatus = "okay";
 	\t\t\t#address-cells = <1>;
 	\t\t\t#size-cells = <1>;

```

This should resolve the linker error and allow the test suite to build and pass.
I am now finished with the task.
